50,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"The candidates are A: Maker Workshop, B: Digital Archive Portal, C: Language Learning Circles, and D: Mobile Branch Service. I'm worried about D because of the roads and costs.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"B is risky; we already failed at digitisation six years ago. C is a better model, as those groups survived.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Shion,,A is impossible without a certified technician for the tools. C requires facilitators we can't supervise.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Minako,,"D's running costs are too high. B's contractors are unreliable. A uses the endowment for equipment, which is safer.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"D is the only one that helps the people who lost their bus links. They can't get to A, B, or C.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Daisuke, but if the roads close and the budget is thin, will the mobile service actually run?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, if A requires a certified technician and Shion says we don't have one, isn't A a dead end?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Minako"",""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Shion,,"Precisely. Unless we hire someone, the Maker Workshop is just a room of dangerous tools.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, we could use the endowment for a new hire or certification. But C's session fees are a budget trap.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Yumi, even with road closures, a mobile service is better than nothing for those wards.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"I think C is the most positive, but I'm scared of the timetable falling apart.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,C has a proven track record of longevity in this system. It's the most logical choice.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Shion,,I can't support A or C. B is too slow. D is the only one that doesn't require specialized staff supervision.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Minako,,D is a financial drain. B is a logistical mess. A is the most stable if we fix the certification.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I'm voting for D. We have to reach the outer wards.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,4,talk,Yumi,,I'll go with C. It's friendly and community-focused!,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I vote for C. The historical data supports it.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,4,talk,Shion,,I vote for D. It avoids the staffing gaps.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,4,talk,Minako,,I'll vote for A. It's the best use of the endowment.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,D is my choice.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
